{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>How many are the days of the years of your life.</b> You look very old and full of days. Jacob answered him: do not wonder at this, for the days of the years of my life have been few; rather, because they were bad, the days of the years of my life, I look old beyond my years. And it is found in the midrash: why were Jacob's years fewer than his father's by thirty-three years? HaShem said to him: I saved you from Laban and from Esau and from Shechem, and I restored Dinah and Joseph to you, and you said, 'few and bad were the days of my life' — I will take away from your years corresponding to the count of the words you spoke, and they are the thirty-three words from <b>Pharaoh said to Jacob</b> until 'the days of their sojournings.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:54.287834896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}